    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-30" id="fn-30" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">PSE re-evaluated it's deferred tax liability in December 2017 due to the 2017 Tax reform and has requested deferral accounting in a petition filed with the Washington Commission on December 29, 2017.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-31" id="fn-31" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Shookumchuck Wind Energy Project accrual on liquidated damages.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-32" id="fn-32" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Included in Washington Commission Docket UE-190606 effective August 29, 2019. On July 16, 2019, PSE filed with Washington Commission an application seeking a determination that 7.74 acres at its Shuffleton Switching Station Property will no longer be necessary or useful under WAC 480-143-180, and authorization for accounting treatment for the gain on sale will be recorded in FERC Account 254 (Other Regulatory Liabilities).</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-33" id="fn-33" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">To record the cost recovery of natural gas costs associated with the Climate Commitment Act in Gas Schedule 111.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-34" id="fn-34" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Included in Washington Commission Docket UE-220066 and UG-220067. Amortize regulatory liability, beginning January 2024, concurrent with rates that are charging customers for costs associated with Colstrip D&amp;R, through the Colstrip Tracker.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-35" id="fn-35" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">As part of PSE's transfer of its interest in Colstrip Units 3 &amp; 4 on January 1, 2026 consistent with CETA and as approved in UE-240729, PSE no longer has O&amp;M costs which requires recovery through a tracker mechanism.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-36" id="fn-36" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">TEP program costs in UE-220066 were removed from the settlement revenue requirement and included in tracker rate Schedule 141TEP in March 2023.&#160; Credit balances are transfered to a regulatory liabilty account.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-37" id="fn-37" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">To record monthly investment tax credit (ITC) amortization beginning in Q3 2025 until the amounts are passed back in Schedule 95A.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-38" id="fn-38" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">To record the pass back of natural gas proceeds associated with the Climate Commitment Act in Gas Schedule 111.</link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-39" id="fn-39" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">Included in Washington Commission Dockets UG-230393 effective May 2024. To record LNG deferrals for Schedule 141LNG Tracker to recognize the difference between the 141LNG tracker revenues from customers, and the components it is recovering (return on rate base, tracker depreciation, O&amp;M, and the amortization of previously deferred return, O&amp;M and depreciation).</link:footnote>
